From: xob0t <32616886+xob0t@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:06:46 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 08/22] Virtual calls through a class pointer merged from
 several ways in

The compiler moves the read of an object's class pointer for a virtual call into
the code before a point where several ways meet (each way reads the class and
sets up its own arguments, one call follows), so the call takes its method from
a merged value: it came out as "__call_indirect(__load8(m0 + off), ...)" with
"ObjKlass value used as data". An address based on such a merge is now the
class of the object when every way in read the class of the same object, or the
class of the merged receiver when each way read the class of the object that
another merged value is given on that way in; merges of such merges count too.
The merged value itself is not read, so its copies go.

What cannot be said about a value as the copy into a merged value (a class
pointer is no data) is now held with the merged value rather than with the value:
it counted before as soon as the value was used for real anywhere (the class's
methods read through it), leaving a Note with no marker in the body.

REWIND_NO_MERGED_KLASS and REWIND_NO_COPY_PROBLEMS_ON_PHI turn these off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
